{"slug": "flip-flop-types-sr-jk-d-t", "question": "What Are the Types of Flip Flop?", "body_html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">The types of flip flop are SR, JK, D and T. Each stores one bit and changes state only on a clock edge.</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0 4px;font-size:16px;\"><tr style=\"background:#1a2b4a;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Type</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Inputs</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Behaviour</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Best For</th></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">SR</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">S, R</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Set, reset or hold; S=1, R=1 is invalid</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Basic memory, debounce</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">JK</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">J, K</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">J=1, K=1 toggles, no invalid state</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Counters, dividers</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">D</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">D</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Q copies D on the clock edge</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Registers, data storage</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">T=1 toggles, T=0 holds</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Binary counters</td></tr></table>"}